## STL build artifacts
*.stl
*.png

## OpenSCAD
*.bak

## Editor
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

## Secrets / keys — never commit
## firmware/.gitignore already lists main/secrets.h; this root rule
## catches any future module-local secrets.h and protects against a
## `git add -A` from the repo root that would otherwise miss the
## firmware-level rule on a typo.
**/secrets.h
**/secrets.local.h
.secrets/

## Build/tool outputs that should stay local
firmware/sdkconfig.prod

## timelapse-tooling outputs — generated MP4s (100+ MB each) and their
## contact-sheet JPEGs. Per-run artefacts rebuilt from the archive on
## demand; never source. Patterns are dir-agnostic (runs default to cwd).
timelapse_*.mp4
timelapse_*_sheet.jpg

## Runtime / rotating logs — host-side processes (HA-MCP server,
## ad-hoc diagnostic scripts) drop into logs/. Per-host operational
## output, not source. Previously committed copies leaked IPv6
## addresses + Python tracebacks; tracked copies removed via
## `git rm --cached` alongside this rule.
logs/

## Per-host IDE/agent scratch
.clangd
.opencode/

## HIL test artifacts — JPEG sweep + ad-hoc capture output. ~6 MB and
## up; not source. Test runs produce a fresh dated subdir per sha so
## tracking would just balloon the history.
firmware/tests/hil/output/

## firmware-test-max17048/ is a 144 MB ESP-IDF diagnostic sandbox left
## over from the 2026-05 fuel-gauge investigation. The conclusion was
## "switch to INA226 + SOC FSM" so this tree is no longer load-bearing
## — kept locally as field-investigation reference but never committed.
firmware-test-max17048/
